    "text": "# **3.2.1 Reaction network** \n\nModel B accounts for the reactions, \n\nR1 : TrkA + NGF _→_ TrkA:NGF _,_ rate = _k_ 1[TrkA][NGF] _,_ R2 : TrkA:NGF _→_ NGF + TrkA _,_ rate = _k_ 2[TrkA:NGF] _,_ R3 : Ras:GDP _→_ Ras:GTP _,_ rate = _k_ 3[TrkA:NGF][Ras:GDP] _,_ R4 : Ras:GDP _→_ Ras:GTP _,_ rate = _k_ 4[Ras:GDP] _,_ R5 : Ras:GTP _→_ Ras:GDP _,_ rate = _k_ 5[Ras:GTP] _,_ R6 : Raf _→_ pRaf _,_ rate = _k_ 6[Ras:GTP][Raf] _,_ R7 : pRaf _→_ Raf _,_ rate = _k_ 7[pRaf] _,_ R8 : Mek _→_ pMek _,_ rate = _k_ 8[pRaf][Mek] _,_ R9 : pMek _→_ Mek _,_ rate = _k_ 9[pMek] _,_ R10 : Erk _→_ pErk _,_ rate = _k_ 10[Erk] _,_ R11 : pErk _→_ Erk _,_ rate = _k_ 11[pErk] _,_ \n\nand the mass conservation \n\n[TrkA] + [TrkA:NGF] = [TrkA]0 [NGF] + [TrkA:NGF] = [NGF]0 [Ras:GDP] + [Ras:GTP] = [Ras]0 [Raf] + [pRaf] = [Raf]0 [Mek] + [pMek] = [Mek]0 [Erk] + [pErk] = [Erk]0 _._ \n\nNote that we do not distinguish between c-Raf and B-Raf. \n\n# **3.2.2 Reaction rate equation and parametrization** \n\nUnder the assumption that the total NGF concentration is much larger than the total TrkA concentration, [NGF]0 _≫_ [TrkA]0, the dynamics of TrkA:NGF, Ras:GTP, pRaf, pMek and pErk can be stated as \n\n\n\nwith kinetic parameters _k_ = ( _k_ 1 _, k_ 2 _, k_ 3 _, k_ 4 _, k_ 5 _, k_ 6 _, k_ 7 _, k_ 8 _, k_ 9 _, k_ 10 _, k_ 11 _,_ [TrkA]0 _,_ [Ras]0 _,_ [Raf]0 _,_ [Mek]0 _,_ [Erk]0 _, s_ ). As the absolute concentrations of TrkA, Ras, Raf, Mek and Erk are unknown, this system is structurally non-identifiable. To circumvent this we reformulate the system in terms of _x_ 1 = _k_ 3[TrkA:NGF], _x_ 2 = _k_ 6[Ras:GTP], _x_ 3 = _k_ 8[pRaf], _x_ 4 = _k_ 10[pMek] and _x_ 5 = _s_ [pErk], yielding the RRE model \n\n\n\n5 \n\n"
